-- the same molecule with a spectrum in which the two methyl classes coincide. The resolved shifts of
-- valine are 0.97 and 0.94; this assignment puts both methyl classes at 0.94, which is what a lower
-- field, a broader line or a different solvent produces, and what happens outright in many molecules
-- whose diastereotopic groups are not resolved. Everything else is the random-coil table: amide 8.44,
-- alpha 4.18, beta 2.13.
vln-shift-coincident : Vln → Nat
vln-shift-coincident x = case x of
  vl-c1 → 0
  vl-o1 → 0
  vl-o2 → 0
  vl-ho → 500
  vl-ca → 0
  vl-ha → 418
  vl-n → 0
  vl-hn1 → 844
  vl-hn2 → 844
  vl-cb → 0
  vl-hb → 213
  vl-cg1 → 0
  vl-g11 → 94
  vl-g12 → 94
  vl-g13 → 94
  vl-cg2 → 0
  vl-g21 → 94
  vl-g22 → 94
  vl-g23 → 94
